<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>Mamaearth returns and growth intelligence</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/styles.css"></head>
<body><header><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">Data Analytics Capstone · 2026</p><h1>Returns and growth intelligence</h1><p>Verified results from the supplied order data. Figures represent discounted order value, not profit or refunds.</p></div></header>
<main class="wrap">
<nav aria-label="Sections"><a href="#overview">Overview</a><a href="#returns">Returns</a><a href="#trend">Revenue trend</a><a href="#narrative">Narrative</a><a href="#sql">SQL reports</a><a href="#quality">Data quality</a></nav>
<section id="overview"><h2>Revenue reconciliation</h2><div class="cards">
<article><small>Raw order value</small><strong>₹{{ '{:,.2f}'.format(findings.raw_total_revenue_inr) }}</strong><span>180 original orders</span></article>
<article><small>Duplicate adjustment</small><strong>−₹{{ '{:,.2f}'.format(findings.duplicate_reconciliation_delta_inr) }}</strong><span>Five repeat submissions</span></article>
<article><small>Cleaned order value</small><strong>₹{{ '{:,.2f}'.format(findings.cleaned_total_revenue_inr) }}</strong><span>175 unique orders</span></article></div>
<p>The five removed records account for the full difference. Missing discounts were treated as zero and missing ratings filled with the median; neither changed order value.</p></section>
<section id="returns"><h2>Where returns concentrate</h2><div class="split"><div><p>COD orders had a <strong>{{ findings.return_rate_by_payment.COD }}% return rate</strong>. The highest-risk group was COD in Tier-2 cities at <strong>{{ findings.highest_risk_segment.return_rate_pct }}%</strong>. These are observed associations, not proof that a payment method causes returns.</p><table><caption>Return rate by payment method</caption><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Orders</th><th>Returned</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for row in rates %}<tr><td>{{ row.payment_method }}</td><td>{{ row['count'] }}</td><td>{{ row.return_rate_pct }}%</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div><img src="assets/return_rate_by_payment.png" alt="COD has the highest return rate at 44.4 percent, followed by UPI at 18.9 percent and Card at 14.7 percent"></div>
<details><summary>View payment and city-tier segments</summary><table><thead><tr><th>Payment</th><th>Tier</th><th>Orders</th><th>Return rate</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for row in segments %}<tr><td>{{ row.payment_method }}</td><td>{{ row.city_tier }}</td><td>{{ row['count'] }}</td><td>{{ row.return_rate_pct }}%</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></details></section>
<section id="trend"><h2>Revenue trend after flagging bulk orders</h2><p>Two unusually large January orders create an apparent January peak. Excluding those orders <em>for the trend comparison only</em> makes March the highest month at <strong>₹{{ '{:,.2f}'.format(findings.true_peak_month.revenue_inr) }}</strong>. The cleaned total above still includes those orders.</p><img class="wide" src="assets/monthly_revenue_trend.png" alt="Monthly order value excluding two bulk orders; March 2026 is the peak at 20,318.90 rupees"><table><caption>Monthly order value in INR</caption><thead><tr><th>Month</th><th>Including bulk</th><th>Excluding bulk</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for row in monthly %}<tr><td>{{ row.month }}</td><td>₹{{ '{:,.2f}'.format(row.raw) }}</td><td>₹{{ '{:,.2f}'.format(row.corrected) }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></section>
<section id="narrative"><h2>Business narrative</h2><p class="muted">Generated via {{ narrative.source }} using validated findings.</p><div class="narrative">{{ narrative.narrative }}</div></section>
<section id="sql"><h2>Raw SQL reports</h2><p>These results come from the unchanged CSVs loaded into SQLite. They intentionally include the five duplicate records.</p>{% for report in reports %}<details><summary>{{ report.title }}</summary>{% if report.rows %}<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr>{% for key in report.rows[0] %}<th>{{ key.replace('_',' ') }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr></thead><tbody>{% for row in report.rows %}<tr>{% for value in row.values() %}<td>{{ value }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>{% else %}<p>No rows.</p>{% endif %}</details>{% endfor %}</section>
<section id="quality"><h2>Data quality and checks</h2><p>Removed duplicate IDs: {{ dropped | join(', ') }}. Quantity outliers flagged and retained: {% for row in outliers %}{{ row.order_id }} ({{ row.quantity }}){% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.</p><ul>{% for label,passed in checks.items() %}<li><span>{{ label }}</span><strong>{{ 'PASS' if passed else 'FAIL' }}</strong></li>{% endfor %}</ul></section>
</main><footer><div class="wrap">Mamaearth capstone · Generated from the project pipeline</div></footer></body></html>
